// Example Wieserlabs DDS script with timed ramp execution
//
// This script demonstrates the new timing control for DDS commands.
// Commands can now include an optional delay:X parameter (in seconds) that
// specifies when the command should execute relative to the start of the script.
//
// Syntax for commands:
//   tone channel frequency amplitude [phase] [delay:X]
//   ramp channel start_freq end_freq amplitude duration [phase] [delay:X]
//   off channel [delay:X]
//
// All frequencies are in MHz, amplitude is 0.0-1.0, phase is in degrees.
// Delays are in seconds.

// Example 1: Single tone on channel 0, executed immediately (no delay)
tone 0 80 0.5 0

// Example 2: Frequency ramp on channel 1 starting after 0.5 seconds
// Ramps from 100 MHz to 150 MHz over 1.0 second with 0.7 amplitude
ramp 1 100 150 0.7 1.0 0 delay:0.5

// Example 3: Another tone with delay
// Turns on 120 MHz on channel 0 after 2 seconds
tone 0 120 0.6 0 delay:2.0

// Example 4: Turn off channel 1 after the ramp completes (1.5 second total: 0.5 sec delay + 1.0 sec ramp)
off 1 delay:1.5
